    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (78.78). **Gunnar Henderson** is our top play, benefiting from a massive +16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Civale. His elite batting order position and dynamic platoon advantage make him the anchor of the lineup, despite a minor efficiency drag from facing a catcher with a quick pop time. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** remains a premium start against Strider; while the opposing arm is formidable, the massive SP skill bonus (+17%) and the stability of the #4 spot make him a must-start for our core production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.41) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) also project for elite days, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizing on a soft matchup against Kochanowicz and **Jackson Merrill** leveraging his BvP history and a prime leadoff spot to offset his slightly lower raw park projections.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Brady House** (54.99). He was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his path was blocked by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who offers a superior +14% dynamic platoon edge against Junk. While **Brady House** has the right profile, the model preferred the established efficiency of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and the high-upside play of **Andy Pages** (67.33), who similarly benefits from a strong SP skill bonus against Strider. Our depth remains robust, but we are keeping a close eye on the risk profile of **Coby Mayo** (55.64); despite the park boost, his #8 spot and negative platoon impact cap his efficiency, keeping him squarely in the \"marginal\" category for today.\n\nOwners should note that while most projections remain stable, any shifts in the confirmed lineups for **Drake Baldwin** or **Liam Hicks** could impact their order-dependent bonuses. We are proceeding with the full lineup as listed, but we are wary of the aggressive base-stealing prevention measures of opposing batteries, which slightly dampened the outlook for speed-reliant players like **Jackson Merrill**. If weather reports in the late windows turn volatile, we are prepared to pivot to the bench, though for now, the data supports aggressive deployment across our primary utility slots.",
